{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q27254078","formula":"C₁₃H₁₇NO₂","hill":"C13H17NO2","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":13.0,"H":17.0,"N":1.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"Encyprate"},"descriptions":{"en":"Encyprate is a monoamine oxidase inhibitor (MAOI) agent that was developed for use in the treatment of depression. It is an irreversible inhibitor of the MAO enzyme because it is agent that can form covalent bonds with the active site. As such, it is sometimes referred to as a “suicide inactivator” of MAO. It was invented by Bruce Horrom of Abbott in the 1960s by structure activity studies on pargyline."},"fame":1,"pubchemCid":17298,"mass":219.28,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCOC(=O)N(CC1=CC=CC=C1)C2CC2","inchikey":"OGXBVBBMMWSZJO-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"ethyl N-benzyl-N-cyclopropylcarbamate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"17298","atoms":33,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-2.513,"y":-0.57,"z":-0.284,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.151,"y":-1.641,"z":1.212,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.623,"y":0.499,"z":0.467,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.988,"y":1.625,"z":-0.368,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.332,"y":2.25,"z":-0.242,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.109,"y":2.987,"z":0.219,"el":"C"},{"x":0.601,"y":0.629,"z":1.245,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.409,"y":-0.656,"z":0.524,"el":"C"},{"x":1.802,"y":0.13,"z":0.487,"el":"C"},{"x":2.176,"y":-1.202,"z":0.598,"el":"C"},{"x":2.52,"y":1.01,"z":-0.311,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.378,"y":-1.711,"z":-0.291,"el":"C"},{"x":3.289,"y":-1.664,"z":-0.104,"el":"C"},{"x":3.633,"y":0.548,"z":-1.013,"el":"C"},{"x":4.018,"y":-0.789,"z":-0.91,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.536,"y":-1.446,"z":-1.23,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.572,"y":1.55,"z":-1.367,"el":"H"},{"x":-3.016,"y":1.913,"z":0.528,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.817,"y":2.595,"z":-1.147,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.77,"y":3.825,"z":-0.377,"el":"H"},{"x":-1.001,"y":3.13,"z":1.287,"el":"H"},{"x":0.49,"y":0.0